  "fluff": {
    "overview": "<p>The Castrum is a Pocket WarShip produced by Boeing Interstellar for the Republic of the Sphere. Entering service in the early thirty-second century, the Castrum was designed to provide the Republic's nascent navy with a domestically produced capital-capable combat vessel at a fraction of the cost and construction time of a true WarShip. The design reflects the Republic's pragmatic approach to naval power, fielding a vessel that could credibly threaten larger warships while remaining affordable enough to produce in meaningful numbers. The Castrum quickly became a key component of the Republic Armed Forces' naval doctrine.</p>",
    "capabilities": "<p>The Castrum is a military spheroid Pocket WarShip mounting a mixed battery of sub-capital and conventional weapons systems. Its primary anti-ship armament consists of sub-capital cannons and missile launchers capable of engaging WarShip-class targets, supplemented by an extensive array of conventional weapons including PPCs, Gauss rifles, and laser batteries for engaging smaller vessels and aerospace fighters. Heavy Ferro-Aluminum armor provides substantial protection for a vessel of its class, allowing the Castrum to absorb considerable punishment during fleet engagements. The drive system provides adequate acceleration for fleet operations, though the Castrum cannot match the speed of lighter escort vessels. The design incorporates fighter bays and marine quarters, giving it force projection capabilities beyond its direct firepower. Anti-missile systems provide point defense against incoming ordnance. The Castrum's primary tactical advantage lies in its ability to bring capital-grade weapons to bear without the enormous expense and crew requirements of a true WarShip, though it remains vulnerable to concentrated fire from dedicated capital ships.</p>",
    "deployment": "<p>The standard Castrum Pocket WarShip serves in its baseline combat configuration as the Republic Armed Forces' primary domestically produced capital-capable vessel. These ships typically operate in small squadrons, providing anti-ship capability to task forces that would otherwise lack any counter to WarShip-class threats.</p>",
    "history": "<p>The Castrum was developed during the early decades of the Republic of the Sphere as part of that nation's effort to build an independent naval capability. Having inherited a mixed fleet of aging WarShips and captured Blakist vessels following the Jihad, the Republic recognized that maintaining and replacing these capital ships was unsustainable. Boeing Interstellar was contracted to develop a more practical solution that could be produced at existing facilities.</p><p>The resulting design drew on lessons learned from the Jihad, where Pocket WarShips had proven capable of influencing fleet engagements at a fraction of the cost of true capital ships. The Castrum entered production at Boeing facilities, with initial deliveries going to the Republic Navy's core formations defending Prefecture X and the capital world of Terra.</p><p>As the Republic began its withdrawal behind Fortress Republic in the 3130s, the Castrum took on increased importance as one of the few combat vessel classes still in active production. The surviving fleet was concentrated within the Fortress walls, where these Pocket WarShips formed a critical layer of the Republic's naval defense. Their capital-grade armament gave the Republic meaningful deterrent capability against any force attempting to breach the Fortress barrier.</p>",
    "manufacturer": "Boeing Interstellar",
    "primaryFactory": "New Earth"
  }
